From f141fa620ad3e8f7e4529151b4708c7bf8ee057f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:36:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] BOOTWAIT_SCREEN (default on with BOOTWAIT): show the
 connection wait on the Z's screen
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Z's Linux reads HDS LBA 0-31 (signature, IPL, partition table, SCSI
driver) in one 16 KB readahead and serves soft resets from that cache,
so anything fake returned there while the HDS is down stays for the
whole power cycle. So:

- After each successful open of the boot HDS (ID 0), compare LBA 0-31
  with a snapshot in flash at 0x1e0000 (4 KB header + 16 KB, keyed by the
  config HDS path and file size, FNV-1a over the data; header written
  last) and rewrite it only when different. Done before the open handle
  is published to the USB task. Writes go through flash_safe_execute.
- While the HDS is not open and a valid snapshot exists for that path,
  serve LBA 0-31 from it exactly, except LBA 2 (IPL) = driver/bootwait1.S
  and LBA 3 = zeros. Without a snapshot: 0014's NOT READY as before.
- bootwait1.S keeps the ROM's d4, loads the waiter (driver/bootwait.S,
  < 4 KB, static) from ID 6 LBA 0x80 to $2800 and jumps there.
- The waiter shows "Pico: SMB 接続待ち… (Wi-Fi/SMB を確認してください)",
  the Wi-Fi/SMB state, the Pico's IP, elapsed seconds and a spinner, and
  polls ID 6 LBA 0x40000-0xfffff every 0.5 s at a fresh, time-derived,
  32 KB-apart slot. Replies (src/bootwait_proto.h) echo the LBA and the
  Pico's uptime so cached old answers are ignored.
  - HDS open and equal to the snapshot: the reply carries the real IPL
    (from the snapshot) and its checksum; the waiter copies it to $2000,
    restores d4 and jumps.
  - HDS different: "HDS が変わりました。Z の電源を入れ直してください" and
    stop (never boot with a stale partition table); the snapshot is
    updated for the next power-on.
  - F1: the setting menu, as hdsboot.S.
- status: snap=none|stored|ok|updated|served|changed.
- test/bootwait: waiter_test.py runs both IPL halves on Unicorn (68000)
  against the real bootwait.c built for the host, with a Linux-like
  page cache: snapshot write/reuse/keying/corruption, wait -> ready
  chain-load with d4, changed -> stop, SCSI errors, stale cached replies,
  F1, HDS missing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
